A||N||4||TRL46202||Quick headlight question....||||1||
Z||000000||TRL46202||09-20-2000||10:13 AM||||Driver side headlight works if helped up by hand. The black dial on top just spins and spins and spins. I can turn it a certain way and the light will go up on its own, but only once. No problems going down. Help<P>Thanks, Tom||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-20-2000||10:52 AM||||motor needs rebuilt.<P>parts are available from <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||HugGRRRFiero||09-20-2000||10:53 AM||||I had the same problem with the drivers side headlight on mine before.  A few months of turning the knob to help it go up it stopped working.  Don't know what exactly causes the problem because I just replaced the motor with another one.  I figure you'll need to tear the motor down to find out what's causing the problem or find another.  Rodney Dickman offers headlight rebuild kits with instructions at  <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/</A>   Check under his electrical products.  <P>Search the forum using headlights as your keyword and you'll find lots more info too.<P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">        <BR>        <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||09-20-2000||12:51 PM||||I'll be darned (said the sock).  Another case  where the driver's side HL went first.<P>If you have 1987-later car, the rebuild is easy.  1984-86 is more difficult. Usually, if I have to rebuild one headlight motor, I plan on doing the other one, too.    ||||reg||10
Z||000004||ROB MAC||09-20-2000||04:05 PM||||The problem is likely the brushes are nearly worn out on the actuator switch. If you can get a new one , it's an easy swap. Don't let the word REBUILD scare you.||||reg||1
